debos-toolbox (0.6.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rebuilt from scratch in Python 3 + GTK 4 (PyGObject) - the native Debian
    desktop toolkit, as used by GNOME Tweaks, Ubuntu Cleaner and Ubuntu Tweak.
  * New design combining soft neumorphic cards, a profile sidebar, colourful
    dashboard tiles, a launcher-style app grid with search and keyboard hints,
    blue gradient buttons, light and dark themes.
  * Embedded task console (VTE) with a queue; tasks run as readable scripts,
    per-step status, Ctrl+C stop, external-terminal fallback.
  * Administrator rights through pkexec (polkit action with auth_admin_keep),
    sudo or su - works when the user is not in the sudo group (Debian default
    when a root password is set).
  * New: Recommendations engine with health score and "Fix all (safe)".
  * Cleaner rewritten (Scan/refresh + Clean): APT cache, unneeded packages,
    old kernels, leftover kernel module folders, package configs, journal,
    rotated logs, crash dumps, /var/tmp, kernel build trees (never while a
    build runs), Flatpak runtimes and caches, thumbnails, Trash, recent
    files, developer caches and browser caches.
  * Kernels: fixed the kernel.org build. Task scripts exported ARCH=amd64,
    which made Kbuild look for arch/amd64 and fail at once (it also broke
    DKMS module builds); ARCH is no longer exported. fakeroot is installed,
    x.y releases (6.12 builds as 6.12.0) are found after the build, every
    build gets its own package revision, localmodconfig no longer fails
    under pipefail, plus disk-space and signature checks, debug info and BTF
    off, bindeb-pkg .deb packages, Ctrl+C stops the build. Kernels installed
    outside APT (made by "make install" in Debos 0.4) are now detected and
    can be removed; XanMod via deb822, Liquorix via extrepo, Debian RT and
    backports kernels.
  * Tasks whose steps depend on each other (kernel builds, vendor
    repositories, login manager switch) stop at the first failed step.
  * Repository Doctor: understands APT 3 (trixie and later) and the sqv
    verifier, whose messages the old version did not recognise; duplicate
    entries are merged without losing components and conflicting Signed-By
    values are aligned; missing keys that are already on the system are
    reused, Debian keyrings are restored, then vendor keys and keyservers;
    expired keys are refreshed; legacy trusted.gpg migration; CD/DVD
    entries, dead repositories, wrong architectures and
    --allow-releaseinfo-change after a Debian release. A repository whose
    key was just repaired is no longer disabled as "dead".
  * Repositories page: components, backports, Debian Fasttrack, experimental,
    mirrors, extrepo third-party repositories, other sources and GPG keys.
  * Software Center: 130+ apps; Debian package first, then extrepo vendor
    repositories, vendor repository/.deb, then Flathub; search all Debian
    packages and Flathub.
  * Desktops & WMs: installed (checkmark) and current session detection;
    Debian-packaged DEs, 25 window managers (Sway, Hyprland, labwc, Wayfire,
    river, niri, i3, bspwm, xmonad, dwm, ...) and 11 login managers
    (greetd, Ly, LXDM, XDM, nodm, Arctica, ...), filtered by availability.
  * Drivers: sysfs-based detection with vendor/device IDs and the kernel driver
    in use; NVIDIA via nvidia-detect with Secure Boot MOK enrollment, AMD,
    Intel, Wi-Fi firmware per vendor, SOF audio, microcode, VM guest tools,
    isenkram suggestions.
  * Desktop Tweaks, Startup Apps, Default Apps, Templates & Scripts and
    desktop settings backup/restore (ideas from Ubuntu Tweak).
  * Packaging: polkit policy, AppStream metainfo, hicolor icons, man page.

 -- Hugo Moniz do Rego <hugomonizdorego@gmail.com>  Tue, 03 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0900

debos-toolbox (0.5.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Complete redesign: sidebar navigation, dashboard, cards, light/dark theme.
  * English is the default language; language and theme are remembered.
  * Support for Debian Stable (trixie), Oldstable (bookworm), Testing (forky)
    and Sid; branch detection and a Stable/Testing/Sid switcher (deb822).
  * New pages: Dashboard, Updates & Release, Tweaks & Tools.
  * Fixed crash on Python 3.11 (Debian 12) caused by an f-string syntax error.
  * Fixed crashes when installing/removing desktop environments and WMs.
  * Fixed software recipes that used non-existent package names.
  * Fixed repo repair corrupting deb822 .sources files; removed weak-signature
    override; XanMod repository codename was never expanded.
  * Rewritten Plymouth, login screen, uninstall and network tools.
  * All scripts are logged to /var/log/debos-toolbox.log.

 -- Hugo Moniz do Rego <hugomonizdorego@gmail.com>  Thu, 01 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0700

